so we've been talking about the  us-mexico border wall and immigration  and the so-called crisis that doesn't  exist at this point for months but in a  real bigger sense release four years  since Donald Trump started his campaign  for the presidency and we've seen a  significant goalposts move one that I  call off the field and into the parking  lot which started with Mexico's going to  pay for the wall and it'll be all nearly  2,000 miles of us-mexico border that  went to well taxpayers are going to pay  for the entire wall and we're still  gonna have 2,000 miles of it too  taxpayers are going to pay for 55 miles  of bollards for 1.3 billion in Trump's  not going to shut down government over  it that gave way late last week to this  is a crisis and Donald Trump is  declaring a national emergency the point  of all of this is to create a pretext  for Donald Trump to commandeer money for  the us-mexico border wall from the US  military and to use the military and  construction powers to just force the  wall to be built circumventing the will  of both the American people and of the  House and Senate neither of which is  into authorizing Donald Trump to  actually do this now we've got to break  this down into its component parts to  even have a shot at understanding the  political implications here number one  there is no illegal immigration crisis  and there is no national emergency here  the real emergency is Donald Trump being  President of the United States and using  such mechanisms as national emergencies  to commandeer funding for projects  Congress won't fund this is disgusting  and it cannot be allowed now let's go  through each talking point in defense of  what Donald Trump is doing one defense  of Donald Trump declaring a national  emergency is national emergencies have  been used before there have been dozens  of national emergencies declared it's  really not a big deal to declare a  national emergency  this is ridiculous the reality is that  yes national emergencies have been  declared before but those national  emergencies were in concert with what  Congress authorized funds for and wanted  to do right the Pres  in allegiance with what Congress wanted  declares a national emergency to  expedite certain decisions or to get  money certain places that Congress  agrees with doing this is the opposite  okay  Congress has declined to fund the wall  multiple times and Donald Trump is  declaring a national emergency to get a  rep excuse me to get around Congress to  circumvent Congress that's not what has  happened in the past that defense is  bogus defense number two this is finally  going to get the wall built in  accordance with what Donald Trump  promised during his campaign wrong  during his campaign Donald Trump's  promise was that they would build 1954  miles of wall that's the entire  us-mexico border and importantly that  Mexico would pay for it this will divert  if it works eight billion total dollars  for the wall and it'll come one point  three seven five billion from the deal  that was made last week by Congress to  keep government open three point six  billion will be taken from military  construction including hospitals two  point five billion will come from the  Department of Defense money meant for  countering drug activity and then the  Treasury will provide six hundred  million dollars so this is going to  maybe build a couple of hundred miles  most optimistically it will take years  likely to the end of Trump's presidency  and there is not even the remote  possibility that 1954 miles of border  wall are going to be built I mean like  don't even dream about it but then we  get to what really is the most important  underlying issue here which is there  simply no crisis legally we don't know  what's going to happen Pat there are  going to be lawsuits Democrats have  tactics to stop this but my hope is that  in a court of law  the Trump administration has to actually  prove that there is a crisis and I don't  know how you do it between ten years of  reduced border crossings year after year  the low criminality of undocumented  immigrants the net outflow of immigrants  to Mexico if you are the Trump  administration Pat how do you go to  court and prove that there's even a  crisis here worthy of an emergency  exactly based on the timeline of events  and lack of evidence to suggest that  this is an  national emergency I think there is a  good chance that the court strike this  down but who knows if it goes all the  way up to the Supreme Court  well Trump's buddies Cavanaugh and  Gorsuch are sitting on there so maybe  they'll let his emergency slide through  but there's also a case we made though  if that happens then that's not even so  bad because the next Democratic  president could say hey I think that gun  violence or I think that climate changes  the national emergency and we have to  declare one for those issues too that's  what's been discussed and I do think  that that is a little bit risky but it  is an it is a valid question at least to  be bringing up what does this open up  the door to do most importantly we have  Trump's own words saying he didn't need  to do this I mean here he is from his  declaration speech saying he actually  didn't need to do this but on the wall  they skimmed so I did I was successful  in that sense but I want to do it faster  I could do the wall over a longer period  of time I didn't need to do this but I'd  rather do it much faster and I don't  have to do it for the election I've  already done a lot of wall if it's an  emergency then you need to do it that's  the whole point of emergencies they are  emergencies that need action and most  importantly if it were an emergency  Trump would have done it two years ago  when the problem was worse even by  today's standards than right now if you  could do the wall over a longer period  of time by definition this is not an  emergency and of course Trump is not  behaving like someone who's dealing with  an emergency immediately heading to one  of his golf clubs played a few rounds of  golf was photographed at the omelet  station grabbing an omelet after or  before golfing who knows here is the  most important issue constitutionally if  you're a small government conservative  you should be furious with Donald Trump  because this if allowed is a massive  expansion of government power and of  presidential power because Congress is  meant to be a check on the president if  the president goes around congressional  opposition to build the wall it should  be the nightmare of small government  conservatives and of course  the midst of all of this we see that  Roger stone was in contact with  WikiLeaks we see that Sarah Huckabee  Sanders has been pulled into the Trump  Russia investigation we see Robert  Muller recommending up to 24 years in  prison for Trump's campaign chairman  Paul Manafort potentially an effective  life sentence on him it's all closing in  around Trump he's getting more and more  erratic and in terms of how this will  impact Trump's followers my guess is not  much at all they've already decided on  intuition that the wall is good and the  wall is right they will create post hoc  rationalizations for why the national  emergency is the right thing to do  don't even waste your breath trying to  convince them to change their mind about  Donald Trump

